# Secret. ${SF_SECRETS_DIR}/offsite.env: read ONLY by the `offsite` job (profile offsite). PENDING INFRASTRUCTURE:
# the off-VPS location (a bucket in another failure domain: other provider or account, access separate from the
# VPS) is not chosen yet; every value below is a placeholder and the job refuses to run while endpoint or bucket
# are unset (ops-offsite-sync.sh). No fictional bucket or credential belongs here.
#
# S3-compatible service (private bucket; Brazil preferred; OPS-1/STACK-7 criteria apply to the provider choice).
OFFSITE_S3_ENDPOINT=
OFFSITE_S3_BUCKET=
OFFSITE_S3_PREFIX=salesforce-staging/
OFFSITE_S3_REGION=
# Use an access key that may WRITE (and read back, for the verification) but not delete or overwrite, ideally with
# bucket versioning/object lock, so a compromised VPS cannot destroy the off-site copies. Retention is the
# bucket's lifecycle policy (e.g. expire after 30 days), not this job.
OFFSITE_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
OFFSITE_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
#
# Encryption (one of the two is REQUIRED; otherwise the job refuses):
#  - client-side with `age` (included in the offsite image): the PUBLIC key of a recipient whose private key is kept
#    by the owner, never on the VPS. The object is stored as sf-staging-<UTC>.dump.age; decrypt with
#    `age -d -i <private key file> -o sf-staging-<UTC>.dump sf-staging-<UTC>.dump.age`.
# OFFSITE_AGE_RECIPIENT=age1...
#  - or the owner accepts uploading the plain dump with provider-side encryption only:
# OFFSITE_ALLOW_UNENCRYPTED=1
#
# Verification of the stored copy: `download` (default: re-download and compare sha256) or `size`.
# OFFSITE_VERIFY=download
# Local rehearsal against a non-TLS endpoint only; never for a real provider:
# OFFSITE_ALLOW_HTTP=1
